## The Call button through Twilio (release 35)
Since release 44 calls are made and taken in the browser (below); ringing the staff member''s own cell first is a Program setting, off by default. The release 35 way: **Call** on a staff page rings the staff member''s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then **Call** opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press **Call** (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).

## Calls in the browser (release 44)

Staff, Admins included, make and take calls in the browser of the staff and Admin portals, with the CarmaCars number as caller ID. Staff abroad never use their own international number.

1. **Call** anywhere opens a bar at the bottom left of the page: **Calling ...**, then the timer, **Mute**, **Keypad** and **Hang up**. The browser asks once for the microphone. The call is kept on the person''s history with its length and its recording, as before.
2. A call to the business number rings the browsers of the staff who have a staff page open, by role (customer service and Sales by default), each with **Answer** and **Decline**. Sales sees the caller''s name or the number hidden.
3. Nobody online or nobody answered: the caller hears the message of Program settings and it is a missed call with its task and its text back, like every missed call. With a forward number set, the call goes there instead. Never to a staff member''s own number.
4. **Settings** > **Program**, the phone settings: **Calls in the browser** (on), Whose browser rings (cs, sales; add admin, fleet or finance), **Ring for (seconds)** (25), Nobody answered: forward to (empty), **Nobody answered: the message**, and Ring my own mobile first (the release 35 way, off).

> Good to know: Setting up Twilio once: save the GitHub repository secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (AC...), TWILIO_API_KEY (an API key SID, SK...), TWILIO_API_SECRET (that key''s secret) and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (the account''s Auth Token, which checks every request from Twilio), and TWILIO_CALLER_ID (the business number, for example +12895550123) when it differs from the CarmaCars number of Site settings. The business number must be a Twilio number or a verified caller ID in Twilio. The site makes the TwiML App "CarmaCars browser calls" itself, and points a Twilio business number with no Voice URL at the site. For incoming calls to ring browsers, calls to the business number must reach that Twilio number (buy it in Twilio, or forward to it). Until all is set, **Call** says what is missing.

Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, **Reveal** shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.

## Unanswered

**Leads** > **Unanswered** (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. **Reply** or **Call back** opens the conversation; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, **Unanswered SLA minutes**) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.

## Call recording and transcripts (release 35)

Calls placed from the site''s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.

1. The recording is copied to CarmaCars'' private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).
2. It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.
3. The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter''s, the lead''s, the booking''s and the conversation''s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.
4. The transcript feeds the renter''s and the lead''s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).
5. Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.</p><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-inbox" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The inbox</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> tab, and press <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo&#39;s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write a text and press <b class="gd-ui">Send text</b>: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a reply</b> puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Stop texts</b> stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unknown-callers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unknown callers</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Unknown callers</b>. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b>, or find the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">Link to</b> the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. <b class="gd-ui">Match automatically again</b> undoes a link made by hand.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-missed-calls" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missed calls</h2><p class="gd-p">A missed call raises the task &quot;Missed call from ...&quot; for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, &quot;Missed call: text the caller back&quot;), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo&#39;s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-and-texts-on-records" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls and texts on records</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s Messages &amp; history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips <b class="gd-ui">Texts</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b>); an owner&#39;s page has &quot;Calls and texts&quot;. Calls are recorded: each call has its transcript and a one-line summary in the Activity log, and calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded too (below).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-activity-log-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Activity log (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section have one <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking&#39;s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">All</b> shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press <b class="gd-ui">All</b> to go back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type in <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> to find a word in the log; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it away.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">50 lines show at a time: <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> shows the next 50, <b class="gd-ui">Newest</b> goes back to the top.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b>, a text or call from them <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, a chat line <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> is above the log; the note shows in it at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking&#39;s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-quo-contacts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quo contacts</h2><p class="gd-p">Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site&#39;s version is sent again.</li><li>One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.</li><li>A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.</li><li>If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Quo contacts</b>: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and <b class="gd-ui">Sync everyone again</b>. Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;, turn it off.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-booking-texts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking texts</h2><p class="gd-p">Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;: the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>; press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-carmacars-app-links" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The CarmaCars app links</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder&#39;s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, <b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-through-the-site-open-the-pop-up-too-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls through the site open the pop-up too (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A call you place from the site (the Call button, the phone in your browser) opens the pop-up at once with the Call helper, for you only. It says <b class="gd-ui">Your call: on now</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Call ended</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the CarmaCars number that rings the browsers opens the pop-up for everyone it rings (customer service and Sales, as set in Program settings), and for every Admin. When someone answers, it says <b class="gd-ui">On the phone now</b> and the history names who took it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up opens within about a second of the ring: it no longer waits for the 10 second check. Every office role gets it: customer service, Fleet, Sales and Finance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every call through the site is recorded (both sides), turned into text and summarised. On the renter&#39;s page, choose <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> in the Activity log: each call shows the date, in or out, who took it, how long, <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Show the transcript</b> and the summary. The booking&#39;s history shows the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Quo calls show Quo&#39;s recording, transcript and summary there too. When Quo sends no summary, the site writes a one line summary from the transcript.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Calls of the last 60 days that were missing a recording, transcript or summary are looked up once at Twilio and at Quo, a few every five minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-minimize-the-pop-up-and-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Minimize the pop-up, and the Call helper (release 43)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The line at the top right of a call minimizes it to a small chip at the bottom of the page: the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. A click anywhere outside the panel, or Esc, minimizes it too; nothing is closed by accident. Press the chip to open the call again. The cross still closes a call in this browser, and a new call always opens by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Inside each call, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> is for new hires: <b class="gd-ui">Say</b> (the greeting, with the staff member&#39;s first name and the caller&#39;s name and booking when known), a button for each situation with 3 to 6 short steps and links to the right page of their portal, and <b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> puts it away in that browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You write all of it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> (see Settings). <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on the helper takes you there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter page has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal&#39;s renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-call-button-through-twilio-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call button through Twilio (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Since release 44 calls are made and taken in the browser (below); ringing the staff member&#39;s own cell first is a Program setting, off by default. The release 35 way: <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a staff page rings the staff member&#39;s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-in-the-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in the browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff, Admins included, make and take calls in the browser of the staff and Admin portals, with the CarmaCars number as caller ID. Staff abroad never use their own international number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> anywhere opens a bar at the bottom left of the page: <b class="gd-ui">Calling ...</b>, then the timer, <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Hang up</b>. The browser asks once for the microphone. The call is kept on the person&#39;s history with its length and its recording, as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the business number rings the browsers of the staff who have a staff page open, by role (customer service and Sales by default), each with <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Sales sees the caller&#39;s name or the number hidden.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online or nobody answered: the caller hears the message of Program settings and it is a missed call with its task and its text back, like every missed call. With a forward number set, the call goes there instead. Never to a staff member&#39;s own number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, the phone settings: <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser</b> (on), Whose browser rings (cs, sales; add admin, fleet or finance), <b class="gd-ui">Ring for (seconds)</b> (25), Nobody answered: forward to (empty), <b class="gd-ui">Nobody answered: the message</b>, and Ring my own mobile first (the release 35 way, off).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Setting up Twilio once: save the GitHub repository secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (AC...), TWILIO_API_KEY (an API key SID, SK...), TWILIO_API_SECRET (that key&#39;s secret) and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (the account&#39;s Auth Token, which checks every request from Twilio), and TWILIO_CALLER_ID (the business number, for example +12895550123) when it differs from the CarmaCars number of Site settings. The business number must be a Twilio number or a verified caller ID in Twilio. The site makes the TwiML App &quot;CarmaCars browser calls&quot; itself, and points a Twilio business number with no Voice URL at the site. For incoming calls to ring browsers, calls to the business number must reach that Twilio number (buy it in Twilio, or forward to it). Until all is set, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> says what is missing.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, <b class="gd-ui">Reveal</b> shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b> (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call back</b> opens the conversation; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered SLA minutes</b>) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-recording-and-transcripts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call recording and transcripts (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The recording is copied to CarmaCars&#39; private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter&#39;s, the lead&#39;s, the booking&#39;s and the conversation&#39;s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript feeds the renter&#39;s and the lead&#39;s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', 'chapter', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'Every renter, owner, investor, staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## Who gets what

- **Email**: emails only. **Text**: a short text instead of the email. **Both**: a text and the email.
- Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.
- No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.
- Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.
- Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, "Continue your request") are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).
- An additional driver''s or a co-signer''s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.

## A person''s channel

Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card **How we reach them** shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press **Change** to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter''s or owner''s; an investor''s only Admins.

## STOP, START and quiet hours

- A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.
- Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), "CarmaCars: you''re unsubscribed and won''t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe." after STOP, and "CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out." after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.
- The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends "Reply STOP to opt out."
- Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.
- A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.

## The settings and the texts

**Settings**, **Text alerts**: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email''s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.

## Booking start and end

Every booking gets these by itself, by email, text and phone alert (each person''s channel), once each, and again only when the time changes (an extension, a new pickup time):

| When | The renter gets |
| --- | --- |
| The day before pickup | What to bring, where and when |
| About 2 hours before pickup | "See you at 2:00 pm today", the place and what to bring |
| 30 minutes after a pickup nobody recorded | "You''re all set", the return time and place |
| The day before the return | The return time and place, fuel and keys |
| About 3 hours before the return | "Your rental ends at 5:00 pm", fuel, clean, all keys and "Need more time? Extend" with its link |
| At the return time | "Your booking ended at 5:00 pm", return now, or the extend offer |
| 15 minutes late | T13, the late notice |
| 2 hours late | T14, the final notice |

- A booking whose pickup nobody recorded counts as out: it gets the end messages, the late notices and the late tasks like a rental on rent. Its status stays as it is.
- The late notices and the short reminders go from 7 am to 10 pm. Overnight they wait until 7 am; a car returned in the night gets nothing.
- The late panel''s **Send T13** and **Send T14** send the same notices: never twice.
- An insurer-billed booking messages the renter too: they hold the car.
- **Pickup not recorded**: 30 minutes after the pickup time with nothing recorded, Fleet gets the task "Record pickup for CC-xxxxx, or mark no-show" and the field staff of the handover an alert and a text. At 3 hours the Admins get an alert and a task. They close by themselves once the pickup is recorded or the booking is cancelled.
- **Not back**: 15 minutes after the return time with no return recorded, the field staff of the return and the Admins get an alert and a text with the renter''s name and phone, at any hour.
- Each moment has its switch, all on: **Settings**, **Text alerts**, "Booking start and end". The text of each is in the list of texts on the same page.

## Texts a day

Site health on **To do** has **Texts today**: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.

## Phone alerts

Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**; iOS 16.4 or later).

- What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners completed trips, payments, incidents and documents (nothing when a booking comes in or changes: release 41), staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts, leads and hot visitors (customer service and Sales also get the last two).
- Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.
- Your own: **Alerts** > **Settings**.
- On or off for everyone: **Settings**, **Text alerts**, "Phone alerts".
- Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and **Alerts** > **Settings** says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.

## Lead and visitor alerts

Staff get an alert, in the app and on their phone, for what needs a person quickly. They are never emailed or texted, so the daily email limit is untouched. The Admins always get them (every device that turned alerts on, so both of you on the shared Admin account); the rest go to the person it concerns.

| What | Who gets it | Topic |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A new renter lead: the contact form, the phone number box, a discount game claim, the live chat. It names the source. | You, and the person the lead is assigned to; if nobody, customer service and Sales on duty | Leads |
| A request typed into the booking request or contact form and not sent (after the capture delay, 30 minutes) | The same | Leads |
| A new owner lead, including "Website form, unfinished", and again when an unfinished application becomes the 30-minute chase | You, and the Sales person it is assigned to | Leads |
| A visitor turns Hot on Live visitors (analytics consent only, once per visitor per day) | You, and customer service and Sales on duty | Visitors |

1. On duty means someone who had Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes.
2. A lead alert goes at once, at any hour, unless the person turned the **Leads** topic off on that device (**Alerts** > **Settings**).
3. More than 5 lead alerts in 10 minutes become one "N new leads" alert for the rest of that window.
4. Test and verification accounts never get them, and a test address never makes one.
5. The switches are under **Settings** > **Text alerts**, "Staff alerts for leads and visitors", all on. Live visitors'' own "notify hot" switch must also be on for the hot visitor alert.

> Watch out: customer service and Sales are only alerted while on duty. With nobody on duty, only the Admins are alerted; the lead is on Leads for the team in the morning.

## Everything else that alerts you

Every staff alert is one rule: what happens, who gets it and a tier. Urgent: on the phone at once, at any hour. Normal: on the phone, held until the quiet hours end. Digest: a line in **Alerts** only. All are on. What each one is and who gets it: the chapter "Alerts: the bell and your phone".

1. Switch a kind off or change its tier: **Alerts** (the bell) > **Settings**, "Which alerts staff get".
2. The amounts and timings (a payment over $500, passing on an unopened urgent alert after 15 minutes, the briefs, grouping, complaint words): **Settings** > **Text alerts**, "Staff alerts".
3. The App Store and Google Play links are empty until the app is published. When set, phones are asked to download the app instead of turning on browser alerts.
