 the Activity log: press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Show the transcript</b> on a call.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call helper (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Inside every call on the pop-up, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> tells you what to say and do. It is made for your first weeks; press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> when you no longer need it (<b class="gd-ui">Show</b> brings it back).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Say</b>: the greeting to read out, with your first name, and the caller&#39;s name and booking when we know them. Start every call with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What is the call about?</b> Press the button that fits: New booking or price question, Change or extend a booking, Running late or late return, Pick-up and delivery, Deposit and payments, Insurance and protection, Accident or damage, Complaint, Owner wants to list a car, or Job applicant. You get 3 to 6 short steps. Words in bold quotes are what to say; a link opens the right page of your portal. <b class="gd-ui">All situations</b> goes back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>: type a word (deposit, late, cancel, km) for the short answer to the questions callers ask most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The amounts, days and percentages in the steps and answers come from the settings, so they are always the ones in force. Never quote a price from memory: the offer screen works it out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Always finish with <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin writes the greetings, the steps and the answers. Something wrong or missing? Tell an Admin: they change it in Settings and you see it on the next call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s record (<b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>, then Open) has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and the notes are in its Activity log (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>), newest first, each with the date and time, who wrote it and their role. Add a note for every situation: what they asked, what you told them, what happens next. Notes cannot be changed or removed by staff, so write a new note to correct one; an Admin can remove a note with a reason. The notes also show on the caller pop-up and on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-lanes-the-call-button-and-hidden-numbers-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lanes, the Call button and hidden numbers (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each conversation has a lane: <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> for a car on rent, or a pickup, return, delivery or collection within a day; <b class="gd-ui">Customer service</b> for the rest. The inbox has a tab for each. The caller pop-up rings for Fleet first on Fleet&#39;s calls; customer service gets them when no Fleet staff member is on duty or nobody answered within 20 seconds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> places the call in your browser (release 44, below): the customer sees the CarmaCars number, and the call is noted on their history with its length. Until calling from the site is set up, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo as before and says why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sales sees customer numbers hidden, like (647) •••-••00. Use <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> on the page: the number is found on our side. Search by phone still works.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-in-your-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in your browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">You make and take calls in the staff portal, in your browser, on the CarmaCars number. Your own phone number is never used and never shown, wherever you work from.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Use a computer with a headset (or earphones with a microphone) in Chrome, Edge or Safari. The first time you call, the browser asks to use the microphone: press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a booking or any staff page. A bar opens at the bottom left of the page (at the top on a phone): <b class="gd-ui">Calling ...</b>, then the call&#39;s timer once they answer. The customer sees the CarmaCars number. Sales: the number stays hidden, the call goes through all the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">During the call: <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> (for a phone menu that asks you to press a number) and <b class="gd-ui">Hang up</b>. Do not close or reload the page during a call: that ends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Incoming calls: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, your browser rings while a staff page is open (customer service and Sales by default). Press <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. The first person to answer takes the call and the others stop ringing. You see the caller&#39;s name when we know it (Sales: the number hidden).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online, or nobody answers: the caller hears a short message, and it is a missed call with its task, like every missed call. A call is never forwarded to your own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Keep a staff page open during your shift with the computer&#39;s sound on, so you hear the ring.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A call that fails (the microphone not allowed, the connection lost): the bar says what to do. Press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>, fix it and call again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calling-from-the-site-your-mobile-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calling from the site: your mobile (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a request or a booking rings your own mobile first, then connects the person. They see the CarmaCars number, never yours. Sales see the number hidden and call this way only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The first time, with no mobile on your profile, a small window asks <b class="gd-ui">Your mobile number</b>. Type your Canadian or US mobile (10 digits, for example (647) 555-0123) and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and call</b>. No code is texted: it is saved to your profile and the call starts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your phone rings. Answer it: you hear &quot;CarmaCars call. Connecting you now.&quot; and the person&#39;s phone rings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A call that cannot start says why in the same window, with <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b>. Calling from the site not set up: ask customer service or an Admin to call, and tell an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To add your number as a sign-in, use <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sign-in</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>. No code after a minute? Press <b class="gd-ui">Resend the code</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Save it without a code</b>: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'a-handover', 'chapter', 'my-jobs', 'You give the renter the keys only after every check passes. The whole handover is one screen: each part has a green tick once it is done, and the button at the bottom says what is still needed.

> Good to know: The job''s header shows how much of the rental walkthrough the renter has read, for example "Renter''s walkthrough: read 2 of 6 steps". Below 6, walk them through the rest at the car: what to bring, the walk-around, the road rules and the return.

> Watch out: Finish the handover in the app, to the last step. Until the pickup is recorded the renter''s messages and the office''s records are guesses: 30 minutes after the pickup time you get an alert and a text to record it, or to mark a no-show.

## Before you start: the ready check

The first part lists what must be done before the car can go: signed, paid, ID checked, deposit. When everything is ready it is one green line; open **The six checks** to see them.

1. Each line should show a green tick: agreement signed, identity verified, coverage confirmed, additional drivers accepted, the booking holds the calendar, deposit taken.
2. A red line shows what you can do about it right under it (see the next part). Fix it, then press **Check again**.
3. All green? Go on down the screen.
4. Coverage or the calendar not ready? Only the office fixes those: call CarmaCars. Still not ready? Press **Stop: do not release the car**.

![](/guides/img/field-21-handover-01-ready-phone-ecb54c56.jpg "phone; size: 390 410; pins: 1 91.0 63.4")

> Watch out: Never hand over keys if the ready check fails, the renter does not match the photo on file, or they do not have their original licence or the card on file. Stop and call us.

## Fix the ready check on the spot

Most red lines are fixed on your phone, without calling the office. Everything you do is recorded with your name.

1. Agreement not signed: press **Sign now on this device** and hand the phone to the renter. A copy signed on paper is not accepted.
2. Identity not verified: for each driver, press **Take** for the licence front, the back and the selfie. Hold the original licence: tick that the name matches, the photo is the person, it is valid past the return and it is class G2 or G. No expiry on file? Type the licence number and the expiry. Press **The licence checks out**.
3. Deposit not taken: press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their card in Stripe''s secure form; take the phone back and press **Back to the job**.
4. Paid by e-Transfer instead: open **Paid by e-Transfer**, type the reference number from their confirmation and press **Record the e-Transfer**.
5. Paid in cash: open **Paid in cash**, count the amount in front of the renter and press **I received**. Keep the cash apart from your own money and hand it to CarmaCars within 1 business day, as Finance directs: Finance gets a task to collect it from you.
6. Additional driver not accepted: press **Sign now on this device (additional driver)**.

> Tip: An expired licence, a face that does not match or a renter who will not sign: do not fix it. Press Stop and call us.

## The handover, on one screen

With the car already? On the job, **Start the check-in now** acknowledges, starts and opens the screen in one tap.

1. **Renter, licence and card**: three taps. This is the renter named on the booking; you checked the original licence (name, photo, not expired; a photo of a licence is not enough); you saw the physical card with the same last four digits. Something is wrong? Open **Something is wrong** and press what it is: the handover stops and the office is told.
2. **Odometer, fuel and keys**: already filled in when the car reports them (from the Tracker, else from its last report). Check each against the dash and change what differs. Fuel: tap the level on the gauge, in eighths from E to F. Keys: **+** and **−**.
3. **Photos**: 19 photos, one tap each. **Take this photo** always shows the next angle; **All 19 photos** lists them, with **Retake**.
4. **Damage**: nothing new? Leave it. New damage: open it, tap the car diagram where it is, choose Where and Type, press **Add the damage** and take the close-up.
5. **Tracker**: one green line when it reports. If not, **Check again**. The car has to go anyway? Open **The car has to go anyway?**, say why and press **Release without the tracker**: an Admin is told at once.
6. **Review and sign**: the renter reads the summary and signs, then you. **Use this signature** for each.
7. Press **Hand over the keys**. You see "Checked in. The rental has started." The renter gets the photo report by email and in their Documents.

Not everything in yet? The button above it says what is next (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you there. A note for Fleet (anything missing or not clean) is under **Add a note for Fleet**.

![](/guides/img/field-29-handover-09-photos-phone-767ecd4f.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")

> Good to know: You were interrupted? Open the job again: your answers and photos are where you left them.

> Tip: Photos wait on the phone without a connection and upload by themselves when it returns; the count shows what is still uploading. Each photo keeps its time, and the place when your phone allows location. No signal on a step? It says "Answers kept on this phone" and you can go on: press Try again, or they are sent when the signal returns.

## Sign now on this device

The renter (or an additional driver) has not signed the rental agreement yet? They sign on your phone.

1. On the job, press **Sign now on this device**. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.
2. Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press **Photograph: Licence, front** (and the back and the selfie).
3. Press **Hand the device to** and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.
4. They hand the phone back: press **Back to the staff view**. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.

## The agreements at check-in

Both rental agreements follow the check-in.

1. Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-in first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.
2. The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.
3. Already signed online? When you complete the check-in, the "as picked up" copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.
4. The check-in stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.

## The deposit on your phone

Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.

1. Press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their credit card in Stripe''s secure form and press the button with the amount.
2. They see "Hold placed": take the phone back and press **Back to the job**. The ready check shows the deposit taken.
3. A rental longer than the hold limit shows **Save the card on this phone (long rental)** instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.
4. No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.

## Add-ons to put in the car

A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.

1. Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example "Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat").
2. Put every item in the car before the handover. The screen lists them again under the readings.
3. Prepaid fuel: the renter may return the car at any fuel level. Do not charge for fuel at the return.
4. A chauffeur on the booking: Fleet tells you who drives and when.

> Tip: An item missing? Write it under **Add a note for Fleet** and call the office before the handover.

> Tip: The photo count shows "19 of 19 photos taken · all uploaded" when the set is complete. The first photo must show the plate. Open circles on the damage diagram were recorded before; add only what is new.

## On one screen (release 28)

On the booking page the check-in is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. It is under **Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)**; the button above it opens the one-screen handover described here.

## When a check stops the handover (release 33)
When something stops the pickup or the return (the deposit, a signature, the licence, the car''s status) and the trip must go ahead, the job shows **What stops the pickup now** with each check. Press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin approves in one tap and the handover is recorded with the time you entered; add the photos and readings afterwards on the job, as with any handover recorded now.
